chapter.v:
The wilderness 


and the, 


dry land shall be glad; the desert shall rejoice and blossom like the crocus;

Then the 


eyes of, 


the blind shall be opened, and the ears of the deaf unstopped;

then shall 


the lame, 


man leap like a deer, and the tongue of the mute sing for joy. For waters break forth in the wilderness, and streams in the desert;
